{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter S2, read/check paths use operation bindings, but live apply, Git push, ACLI/delivery, and bridge orchestration still rebuild config or reuse broad parent environments. Jira Cloud scope still has implicit `DIG` fallbacks (write path, the live access-check probe, the runtime default, and the create-time default). These paths can write under an unintended scope or leak a Rebar-materialized credential to an unrelated sibling child.\n\n## Outcome\nCut write/apply and subprocess paths over to the S2 runtime. Add one shared child-environment builder: trusted same-capability children start from ambient inheritance, owning children receive their adapter overlay, unrelated siblings remove exact secret names declared by other Rebar adapters, unknown native Git/SSH/AWS/proxy/CA variables survive, and Rebar never mutates global `os.environ`.\n\n## Plan\n1. Thread `ReconcilerSettings`, `GitRuntime`, selected `BridgeRuntime`, and the already-constructed backend through applier, mutation planning/dispatch, inbound/outbound handlers, binding updates, Git adapter/ref/lock/push, and `_bridge_runner` delivery paths. Remove their ambient `load_config`/cwd/default fallbacks.\n2. Add `src/rebar/_child_env.py` with a pure environment projection API and a checked-in registry of exact secret names owned by each Rebar adapter. The registry contains names, never values; native SDK/helper chains remain ambient.\n3. Ensure CLI `-c` tracker/Jira/reconciler selections cross the reconciler subprocess boundary as non-secret snapshot material. Pass static adapter material only to the exact owning process/adapter.\n4. Eliminate every implicit `DIG` Jira-project default so no request (write OR live probe) uses `DIG` unless it is explicitly configured: (a) the write path `resolve_jira_settings(project_default=\"DIG\")` in `adapters/jira/backend.py` (:200/:230/:316); (b) the live access-check probe `JIRA_PROJECT` `or \"DIG\"` in `access_check.py` (:72/:77/:262); (c) the `_CLOUD_PROJECT_DEFAULT = \"DIG\"` constant in `rebar_reconciler/runtime.py` (:46); and (d) the create-time `_DEFAULT_PROJECT = \"DIG\"` in `_store/project_ensures.py` (:50). Each unset case fails closed with a typed/redacted pre-mutation (or pre-probe) error; `DIG` is used only when `JIRA_PROJECT`/config is explicitly `DIG`. Preserve existing retry, rate-limit, TLS, output, partial-failure, idempotency, and ticket-delivery behavior unless a test names the approved delta.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- End-to-end verified-fake Cloud/DC runs cover create/update/comment/link/delete/inbound apply plus Git commit/push/delivery under custom tracker dir/branch/remote with ambient resolvers poisoned after composition.\n- Child-process contract tests assert unknown ambient/native-chain variables survive; the owning overlay appears only for its child; unrelated siblings lose other adapters' exact declared names; argv/URL/log/output contain no secret sentinel.\n- Concurrency tests run distinct operations with different overlays and timeouts, asserting `os.environ` is byte-equal before/during/after and no cross-operation value is observed.\n- Failure-injection tests cover missing project/auth, revoked credential, TLS error, retry/rate-limit exhaustion, provider partial failure, and delivery failure; existing provider-neutral output and recovery/idempotency oracles remain authoritative.\n- A red test demonstrates each current `DIG` default (write path AND the live access-check probe); green asserts zero provider mutation and no probe request targeting `DIG` when write scope is absent.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nUntil bounded-live validation, a compatibility facade may invoke the legacy write path. Before cutover, rollback selects it. After any new snapshot-aware caller ships, rollback requires the S1 envelope-compatible floor. Ticket, event, bridge, and binding formats remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Verified-fake Cloud/DC apply plus Git/delivery paths complete with ambient resolvers poisoned and use the configured tracker directory/branch/remote and explicit project scope.\n- [ ] Missing Cloud write scope produces a typed/redacted pre-mutation failure and no request uses `DIG` unless `DIG` was explicitly configured.\n- [ ] Same-capability child tests preserve unknown Git/SSH/AWS/proxy/CA variables, owning children receive only their overlay, and unrelated siblings omit every other adapter's exact declared secret name.\n- [ ] Concurrent-operation tests prove no global environment mutation and no cross-operation credential/config observation.\n- [ ] Existing retry, rate-limit, TLS, output, partial-failure, recovery, and idempotency scenarios retain their provider-neutral behavior except explicitly approved deltas.\n- [ ] Disabling the write facade restores the legacy path before cutover; no stored ticket/event/bridge/binding format changes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787040433889424001,"uuid":"845a463c-282c-4409-9c6f-ba8177bee868"}